{
  "$comment": "The shape assignments workflow/formal/assign.py CANNOT DERIVE -- that, not who authored them, is why this file exists separately from curated/formal-assignments.json. (Both are AI-authored; the distinction is input vs. output.) For 58 real functions it records which shape fits and how its slots are filled, and assign.py consults it as its first matching rule. Measured 2026-07-22 by re-running assign.py against an emptied seed: 30 of the 58 come out differently without it -- 22 fall from shape_assigned to escalate_new_shape or no_formal_applicable (the whole RMA/window family: mpi_put, mpi_get, mpi_accumulate, all seven mpi_win_*, plus mpi_scatter, mpi_gather, mpi_wait, both split-collective MPI-IO calls, and the alloc/free + comm-init pairs across all four PPMs), and 3 keep a shape but change content (mpi_scan gets a different shape_ref; mpi_recv/mpi_irecv get different slot fills). This is therefore also where a correction belongs if it must SURVIVE: curated/formal-assignments.json is rebuilt wholesale by --regenerate formal, this file is not. The expansion each assignment must produce is a test fixture and lives in workflow/formal/testdata/expansions.json, joined on 'ppm:function'.",
  "$comment_unmatched": "3 of the 58 currently match no corpus entry and so contribute nothing to a build: nvshmem_int_sum_reduce, nvshmem_int_atomic_add, shmem_int_sum_reduce. They are KEPT DELIBERATELY -- they name real functions of their PPMs, so they are evidence of an Extract coverage gap, not dead weight. As of 2026-09-11 the corpus holds 74 NVSHMEM entries, still all untyped *mem variants (broadcastmem, getmem, ...) with none of the typed API; and 279 SHMEM entries containing no reduce operation at all. Deleting these would erase the only in-repo record that assign.py is ready for functions Extract has not yet produced. nvshmem_malloc was a fourth until 2026-09-11, when the NVSHMEM adapter learned the `void *name(...)` and `static inline` declaration forms it had been missing (seven functions, nvshmem_malloc among them) -- exactly the re-check this note asks for whenever Extract's coverage changes. The shmem one may also need the typed-API literal-token convention (shmem_{T}_*) settled first -- see docs/schema/shape-catalog.md's gather_to_all row.",
